 4. 🕯️ Never forget 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Spencer Platt/Getty Images A worker buffs the surface of the September 11 Memorial in New York yesterday ahead of remembrance events on the 25th anniversary of the terrorist attacks.

 The annual remembrance ceremony at Ground Zero will begin at 8:40 a.m. ET. The first of seven moments of silence will be observed at 8:46 a.m., when the first plane struck the north tower of the World Trade Center. 

 The other moments of silence commemorate when the south tower was struck, when each of the towers fell, the attack on the Pentagon, the crash of Flight 93 near Shanksville, Pa., and to honor those who lost their lives to 9/11-related illnesses and injuries. President Trump will speak at a Pentagon ceremony this morning.

 Photo: Craig Barritt/Getty Images for the New York Foundation of the Arts Above: A drone show depicts the Twin Towers using 2,977 lights, one for each life lost on 9/11, on Wednesday during a test of the annual " Tribute in Light ."

