 5. ☎️ Scoop: Saudis urged Trump to strike Houthis 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces clash with the Iran-aligned Houthis in an image released yesterday. Photo: Media Center of Yemeni Armed Forces via Reuters 🛢️ Driving the day: U.S. diesel fuel prices hit another record this morning, soaring past $6 a gallon amid the escalating conflict with Iran. Go deeper .

 Intel from Axios' Barak Ravid : Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman (MBS) called President Trump twice yesterday, urging him to launch strikes against the Houthis as the Iran-backed group closed in on a vital Red Sea chokepoint.

 Trump declined, and U.S. officials stressed the administration has no plans to intervene directly against the Houthis for now. Why it matters: Oil prices surged yesterday as the Houthis seized a strategic coastal city in Yemen, pushing them closer to the Bab al-Mandab Strait — a vital artery for global trade and Saudi oil exports.

 With Iran already disrupting traffic through the Strait of Hormuz, Houthi control of Bab al-Mandab could give Tehran a powerful new point of leverage over the U.S. and its Gulf allies. Keep reading . 

 
 
