 7. 📱 Scoop: TikTok blocks Meta&#x27;s ads 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 TikTok has rejected ads from Meta that call on TikTok and other tech platforms to join Meta in settling with U.S. state attorneys general in a landmark children's safety lawsuit, sources tell Axios' Sara Fischer. 

 Why it matters: Part of Meta's historic multibillion-dollar settlement is contingent on its peers also agreeing to settle. Other tech firms have yet to publicly comment on their plans. Meta has been running a public campaign to encourage TikTok and YouTube to join its settlement through statements and advertisements. Snap Inc., which is notably not mentioned in its campaign, appears poised to settle.

 Meta argues it will face a competitive disadvantage if it's the only platform forced to add restrictions as part of a settlement. Keep reading ... Get Axios Media Trends . 

 
 
